  "主要内容": "In 2015, global M&A reached $5 trillion, with the U.S. accounting for half the volume. Major deals included Anthem (ANTM) and Cigna (CI) merging for $55.2 billion, Energy Transfer Equity (ETE) and Williams Companies (WMB) combining for $55 billion, Cheung Kong Holdings (CHEUY) acquiring Hutchison Whampoa (HUWHY) for $53.1 billion, and HJ Heinz and Kraft Foods merging to form Kraft Heinz Company (KHC) for $62.6 billion. Dell merged with EMC for $66 billion, facing a $9 billion tax liability. Dow Chemical (DOW) and DuPont merged for $68.6 billion. Charter Communications (CHTR) acquired Time Warner Cable and Bright House Networks for $79.6 billion. Royal Dutch Shell (RDS.A) purchased BG Group for $81.5 billion. Anheuser Busch Inbev (BUD) merged with SABMiller for $117.4 billion, the largest merger in history. Pfizer (PFE) merged with Allergan (AGN) for $160 billion, acquiring Hospira for $17 billion. Allergan (AGN) is projected to post top-line expansion of nearly 40% in 2015 due to Botox. Securities explicitly mentioned in the source include BG Group (BRGYY), SABMiller (SBMRY).",
